{"page":44,"verses":[{"verse_key":"2:260","surah":2,"ayah":260,"ar_uthmani":"وَإِذْ قَالَ إِبْرَٰهِـۧمُ رَبِّ أَرِنِى كَيْفَ تُحْىِ ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ ۖ قَالَ أَوَلَمْ تُؤْمِن ۖ قَالَ بَلَىٰ وَلَـٰكِن لِّيَطْمَئِنَّ قَلْبِى ۖ قَالَ فَخُذْ أَرْبَعَةً مِّنَ ٱلطَّيْرِ فَصُرْهُنَّ إِلَيْكَ ثُمَّ ٱجْعَلْ عَلَىٰ كُلِّ جَبَلٍ مِّنْهُنَّ جُزْءًا ثُمَّ ٱدْعُهُنَّ يَأْتِينَكَ سَعْيًا ۚ وَٱعْلَمْ أَنَّ ٱللَّهَ عَزِيزٌ حَكِيمٌ","en_translation_id":85,"en":"And when Abraham said, ‘My Lord, show me how You give life to the dead,’ He said, ‘Do you not believe, then?’ ‘Yes,’ said Abraham, ‘but just to put my heart at rest.’ So God said, ‘Take four birds and train them to come back to you. Then place them on separate hilltops, call them back, and they will come flying to you: know that God is all powerful and wise.’","words":[{"pos":1,"ar":"وَإِذْ","en_gloss":"And when","transliteration":"wa-idh","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":2,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"said","transliteration":"qāla","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":3,"ar":"إِبْرَٰهِـۧمُ","en_gloss":"Ibrahim","transliteration":"ib'rāhīmu","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":4,"ar":"رَبِّ","en_gloss":"My Lord","transliteration":"rabbi","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":5,"ar":"أَرِنِى","en_gloss":"show me","transliteration":"arinī","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":6,"ar":"كَيْفَ","en_gloss":"how","transliteration":"kayfa","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":7,"ar":"تُحْىِ","en_gloss":"You give life","transliteration":"tuḥ'yī","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":8,"ar":"ٱلْمَوْتَىٰ ۖ","en_gloss":"(to) the dead","transliteration":"l-mawtā","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":9,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"He said","transliteration":"qāla","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":10,"ar":"أَوَلَمْ","en_gloss":"Have not","transliteration":"awalam","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":11,"ar":"تُؤْمِن ۖ","en_gloss":"you believed","transliteration":"tu'min","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":12,"ar":"قَالَ","en_gloss":"He said","transliteration":"qāla","verse_key":"2:260"},{"pos":13,"ar":"بَلَىٰ","en_gloss":"Yes","transliteratio